                <pb facs="0985" n="849" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg849"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/525: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Argentina</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-20T18:00:00-04:00">May 20, 1929—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>40. Department’s 37, May 11, 6 p.m. The Commission of Inquiry and Conciliation
                    has arranged for the repatriation of prisoners held respectively by Bolivia and
                    Paraguay. The prisoners held by Bolivia will be brought to Formosa if the
                    Argentine Government consents to a request already made through the Argentine
                    Embassy here for this purpose. When Argentine consent is received the Military
                    Attaché at your Mission will be asked to proceed with an Argentine officer to
                    Formosa to assist in connection with the repatriation. Further instructions will
                    be sent for this purpose.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
